# Copy to hotspot_secrets.properties (gitignored, never commit the
# real password) and fill in your real hotspot SSID/password, then push
# to the phone at /data/adb/dashboard/hotspot_secrets.properties.
#
# Added 2026-07-08 after a real incident: hotspot_on_boot.sh used to
# try reading the SSID/password dynamically from Android's own
# WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml, falling back to a hardcoded value if that
# read failed - and the fallback PASSWORD was a redacted placeholder
# string ("CHANGEME_PASSWORD" in the repo copy) rather than the real
# one, with a comment saying the on-device copy had the real value
# substituted in. That substitution had been lost at some point, and
# since the dynamic XML read had *also* silently stopped working after
# an OS update (confirmed 2026-07-06 - the file doesn't exist on this
# build anymore), the fallback was quietly live-broadcasting
# "CHANGEME_PASSWORD" as the actual hotspot password every time a
# restart triggered fresh config generation - locking out every device
# with no warning, discovered only when it finally happened live
# 2026-07-08. A redacted-placeholder-as-functional-fallback is
# inherently fragile in exactly this way; reading from a real gitignored
# properties file (the same pattern already used for every other secret
# in this project) can't have that specific failure mode - either the
# file has the real value, or it's missing and the script can fail
# loudly instead of silently broadcasting a placeholder as if it were
# real.
HOTSPOT_SSID=PILLYBOO
HOTSPOT_PASSWORD=your_real_hotspot_password_here
